# promise: #547
# A press on the sidebar's empty space under the tabs that moves past 3 pt moves the window, as
# Arc's sidebar background does; a click there moves nothing. The drags go through the event
# queue, as the pointer's would; the window drag itself is the window server's, so the scenario
# reads where it started.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=one
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1

# A click on the empty space: no window drag.
cra://debug?clickAt=120,520
wait 1
reject-log window drag from sidebar

# A drag there: the window's.
cra://debug?dragAt=120,520&by=40,30
expect-log window drag from sidebar empty space
wait 1

# The press is the list's to handle: AppKit's own background drag stays out of the sidebar, so a
# row's drag never moves the window as well.
cra://debug?hitAt=120,520&move=1
expect-log hit at 120,520: SpaceListDocument- <
